#: ../../source/docs/MATLAB-Serial-driver.rst:7
#: 8dffbc78fd61488a9a2120dc9cdca2d1
msgid "The TCP/UDP/IP Toolbox can also be used to interact directly with SITL serial ports. This allows MATLAB to be used to replicate a sensor protocol fore testing and debugging ArduPilot drivers. Unlike previous examples TCP is used and two way communication is possible. By default SITL uses ports 5760 to 5763 for serial ports 0 to 3. The appropriate SERIALx_PROTOCOL parameter should be set to the driver being tested, baud rate is not used. Such a MATLAB tool greatly speeds up development of drivers removing the need to flash and test on real hardware."
msgstr ""

